[0.0, "o", "Investigating REAL data for tenant \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: can i trust our crm data? what is missing or inconsistent in the deals we closed this quarter?\r\n\u001b[2m2026-09-30 10:55:51\u001b[0m [\u001b[33m\u001b[1mwarning  \u001b[0m] \u001b[1mmcp.nothing_admissible        \u001b[0m \u001b[36mlabel\u001b[0m=\u001b[35mposthog\u001b[0m \u001b[36mreason\u001b[0m=\u001b[35m'the server was queried and offered no tool Cortex can admit; every tool must declare readOnlyHint: true'\u001b[0m\r\nRead-only: no write capability exists in the tool registry.\r\nCapabilities available to \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: github, hubspot, posthog, slack\r\n  [  0.1s]          checking what data exists\r\n  [ 12.1s]          found posthog__list_projects\r\n  [ 12.1s]          checking memory for prior context\r\n/Users/nikhil/cortex-oss/cortex/memory/vector_store.py:191: UserWarning: Api key is used with an insecure connection.\r\n  self._client = AsyncQdrantClient(url=self._url, api_key=self._api_key)\r\n  [ 12.2s] step 1   deciding what to look at\r\n/Users/nikhil/cortex-oss/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/qdrant_client/async_qdrant_remote.py:225: UserWarning: Qdrant client version 1.18.0 is incompatible with server version 1.16.3. Major versions should match and minor version difference must not exceed 1. Set check_compatibility=False to skip version check.\r\n  show_warning(\r\n  [ 19.4s] step 1   calling hubspot__closed_won\r\n  [ 19.4s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 19.4s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 19.4s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 19.4s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 21.1s] step 1   got hubspot__closed_won (2 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 21.1s] step 1   got hubspot__search (3 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 21.1s] step 1   got hubspot__search (4 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 21.1s] step 1   got hubspot__search (5 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 21.1s] step 1   got hubspot__search (6 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 21.1s] step 2   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 25.3s] step 2   calling hubspot__companies query='\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'\r\n  [ 25.3s] step 2   calling hubspot__activities\r\n  [ 25.3s] step 2   calling hubspot__companies query='\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'\r\n  [ 27.9s] step 2   got hubspot__companies (7 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 27.9s] step 2   got hubspot__activities (8 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 27.9s] step 2   got hubspot__companies (9 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 27.9s] step 3   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 31.4s] step 3   calling hubspot__activities\r\n  [ 31.4s] step 3   got read hubspot.companies in full (\u2588\u2588 rows) (9 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 36.1s] step 3   got hubspot__activities (10 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 36.1s] step 4   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 40.1s] step 4   calling hubspot__companies query='\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'\r\n  [ 40.1s] step 4   calling hubspot__companies query='\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'\r\n  [ 40.9s] step 4   got hubspot__companies (11 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 40.9s] step 4   got hubspot__companies (12 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 40.9s] step 5   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 42.5s] step 5   got read hubspot.activities in full (\u2588\u2588 rows) (12 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 42.5s] step 6   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 64.7s]          drafting the report from 12 observation(s)\r\n  [105.9s]          checking every citation resolves\r\n  [105.9s]          re-reading each claim against its own evidence\r\n  sufficiency gate: the evidence does NOT support a cause (6.3s); missing: Data quality checks beyond amount/owner/contacts nullity \u2014 e.g. duplicate company records for the same account (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 has 2 entries, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 has 4), verification of which company record is truly linked to each closed-won deal; Field-level audit of deal records themselves (e.g. source_detail consistency, deal_type accuracy, pipeline stage history) rather than just presence/absence of a few properties; Explanation for why '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' company search returns 0 results despite having a closed-won deal \u2014 is this a naming mismatch, unlinked record, or deletion; Historical baseline of data completeness in prior quarters to know if this quarter's gaps are new or typical\r\n  sufficiency gate withheld 1 causal claim(s)\r\n  [122.5s]          writing the report\r\n\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: Can I trust our CRM data? What is missing or inconsistent in the deals we closed this quarter?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: insufficient evidence\r\nTook 106s over 6 steps, 37,741 tokens, 12 observations gathered, 10 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  The four deals closed-won in Q\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 (2026-07-01 through 2026-09-30) are structurally complete at the deal-record level -- none is missing amount, owner, or contact-count -- so the CRM's deal object itself is trustworthy for this quarter.  [hubspot.closed_won 3e5ac58a, hubspot.search b9f81aaf, hubspot.search dd9b00a7, hubspot.search b48b7857]\r\n  The real inconsistency is one level up, at the company object: the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 deal has no linked company record, the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 account is split across four company records including one with entirely blank name and firmographic fields, and the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 account sits inside \u2588\u2588 similarly-named company matches with no engagement history on the record actually marked as the customer.  [hubspot.search bda8f5d7, hubspot.companies ac5b63f0, hubspot.companies c20ed508, hubspot.companies 9711449c, hubspot.activities 28088a81]\r\n\r\nFINDINGS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Deal records themselves are structurally complete  (high)\r\n    - All \u2588 deals closed-won in Q\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 (2026-07-01 to 2026-09-30) have amount, owner_id, and associated-contact-count populated; explicit searches for closed-won deals missing any of these three fields in this window returned zero matches.  [hubspot.closed_won 3e5ac58a, hubspot.search b9f81aaf, hubspot.search dd9b00a7, hubspot.search b48b7857]\r\n  \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: a closed $\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 deal with no company record  (high)\r\n    - The \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 deal ($\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588, closed 2026-08-17) has no matching company in a HubSpot company search for its own name, meaning the deal cannot be tied to a firmographic record at all.  [hubspot.search bda8f5d7, hubspot.companies ac5b63f0]\r\n  \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: duplicate company records with a partially blank one  (high)\r\n    - Four separate company records match '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588': two are the same telecom account under different domains (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 and \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, one marked customer and one still marked lead), one is a distinct reseller (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588), and one has null name, null country, null employee count, and null industry.  [hubspot.companies c20ed508]\r\n    - The \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 deal that closed for $\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 on 2026-09-04 is backed by \u2588\u2588 logged engagements on the primary \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 company record spanning emails, calls, and meetings from June through the close date and beyond, indicating the account activity itself is well tracked even though the company record is duplicated.  [hubspot.closed_won 3e5ac58a, hubspot.activities ffaef59e]\r\n  \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: severe company-record duplication and ambiguity  (medium)\r\n    - A search for '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' returns \u2588\u2588 total matching companies, including two records literally named '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' (one domain \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 marked customer, one domain \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 marked lead) plus dozens of unrelated companies with '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' or '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' in their name that pollute the same namespace.  [hubspot.companies 9711449c]\r\n  Deal source attribution is a mix of manual backfill and real tracking  (medium)\r\n    - Of the \u2588 closed-won deals, \u2588 carry source_detail values of IMPORT, CRM_UI, or \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 rather than a tracked marketing channel, and only one (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) shows an organic-search source with keyword detail, indicating most of this quarter's closed revenue was manually entered or backfilled rather than attributed by the tracking pipeline.  [hubspot.closed_won 3e5ac58a]\r\n\r\nHYPOTHESES TESTED\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  [inconclusive] The \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 deal's company record is simply hard to find because of a large, noisy set of similarly-named companies, not because the record itself is broken.\r\n      The digest and full read both confirm dozens of genuine, distinct companies share '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'/'\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' substrings with '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588', which is a search/naming collision problem rather than evidence the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 record itself lacks data -- the actual \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-named record has full firmographic fields (revenue, employees, industry, country).\r\n  [inconclusive] The zero engagements on the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 company record means the $\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 deal is fabricated or unsupported by real sales activity.\r\n      An empty engagement list is consistent with activity being logged against a different (duplicate) \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 company record, against contacts directly rather than the company, or against deal-level notes not queried here -- it does not by itself establish the deal lacks a sales trail, only that this specific company record shows none.\r\n  [contradicted] Missing/duplicate company records reflect a broken deal-creation pipeline that also produces missing deal fields.\r\n      If deal creation itself were broken, deal-level fields (amount, owner, contact count) would also show gaps. They do not -- all four closed-won deals are complete on those fields. The company-record problems (duplication, missing match, blank fields) are a separate, company-object-specific data quality issue, most likely from lead-gen/enrichment deduplication failing rather than deal entry failing.\r\n\r\nRECOMMENDATIONS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  P\u2588 Confirm which \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 company record the $\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 deal's activity was actually logged against, and if none, investigate whether sales engagement is being logged at all for that account.\r\n      why: The queried \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 company record shows zero engagements against an eight-figure deal that closed this quarter, which is either a data-linkage error or a genuine gap in tracked sales activity -- both need resolving before this figure is used in forecasting.\r\n      [hubspot.closed_won 3e5ac58a, hubspot.activities 28088a81]\r\n  P\u2588 Create or link a company record for the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 deal and audit other closed deals for the same gap.\r\n      why: A closed $\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 deal with no associated company record cannot be rolled up into account-level reporting, ABM attribution, or renewal tracking.\r\n      [hubspot.search bda8f5d7, hubspot.companies ac5b63f0]\r\n  P\u2588 Run a company-object deduplication pass on \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 and \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, merging the customer-stage record with lead-stage duplicates and the blank-field record.\r\n      why: Duplicate and partially blank company records for two of this quarter's four closed deals create ambiguity about which record holds the authoritative firmographic and engagement history, undermining confidence in account-level reporting.\r\n      [hubspot.companies 9711449c, hubspot.companies c20ed508]\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - The engagement search on the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 company was scoped to one specific company id; if sales activity was logged against a duplicate \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 record instead, the true engagement count is understated and the 'no activity found' claim would be an artifact of which duplicate was queried, not a real gap.\r\n  - Company search results are name-matched and may not be exhaustive or precise; total_matching=\u2588\u2588 for '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' was truncated to \u2588\u2588 rows in the initial digest and required a full read to confirm which record was the true \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 account, so similar undetected duplication may exist for other accounts not investigated here.\r\n  - Only \u2588 deals closed in the quarter, so any single anomaly (like the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 missing company) represents \u2588\u2588% of this quarter's closed-won volume -- conclusions about 'CRM trustworthiness' rest on a very small sample and may not generalize to the full pipeline or historical quarters.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) were removed because an independent check found the cited evidence did not support them. Treat the remaining conclusions with corresponding caution.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) go beyond their evidence and are retained with reduced confidence rather than removed, because the rest of each one holds. What the check found:\r\n- executive_summary[0]: The four searches confirm zero deals missing amount, owner, or contact-count, supporting the completeness finding, but the broader inference that 'the CRM's deal object itself is t\r\n- executive_summary[1]: The \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 and \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 company findings match the evidence exactly, but the activities check was run against object_id \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 (the deal ID) not against the actual \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 c\r\n- executive_summary[2]: Evidence shows \u2588 of \u2588 deals have source_detail IMPORT/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/CRM_UI (source=OFFLINE) while one is ORGANIC_SEARCH, supporting the count, but the leap to 'reporting should be tr\r\n- findings[2].claims[1]: The \u2588\u2588 activities spanning June through beyond the close date are confirmed by the activities payload, but the evidence shown includes no indication that the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 company record\r\n  - \u2588 causal claim(s) were withheld: a separate check of the evidence gathered, made without seeing this report, found that it does not support a definitive answer about cause. The observations show the four closed-won deals this quarter and confirm no nulls in amount/owner/contacts fields, plus reveal a company-matching anomaly (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 has no matching company record, and both \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 have multiple ambiguous company entries). This establishes some inconsistencies exist but doesn't \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588atically audit CRM trustworthiness or explain why these gaps occurred, so it can describe symptoms but not deliver a definitive answer on overall data trust or root causes. What would settle it: Data quality checks beyond amount/owner/contacts nullity \u2014 e.g. duplicate company records for the same account (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 has \u2588 entries, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 has \u2588), verification of which company record is truly linked to each closed-won deal; Field-level audit of deal records themselves (e.g. source_detail consistency, d\r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - Company search for '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' initially returned only a computed digest over \u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588 total matching rows; a full read was required to identify the specific record tied to the closed deal, so any figure drawn from an unread digest elsewhere in this investigation should be treated as provisional.\r\n  - Three of the four closed-won deals carry source_detail of IMPORT, CRM_UI, or \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, indicating manual entry or backfill rather than pipeline-tracked attribution, which limits how much the 'source' field can be trusted for channel-level revenue reporting this quarter.\r\n  - The github commits sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github deployments sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github issues sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github links sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog annotations sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog events sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - \u2588 of the \u2588\u2588 cited observation(s) returned no results (hubspot.activities, hubspot.companies). Conclusions resting on them describe what was not found, which is not the same as what does not exist.\r\n\r\nSOURCES\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  28088a81  hubspot.activities  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/engagements\r\n  ffaef59e  hubspot.activities  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/engagements\r\n  3e5ac58a  hubspot.closed_won  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closed_won=2026-07-01..2026-09-30\r\n  9711449c  hubspot.companies  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/search?q=\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\r\n  c20ed508  hubspot.companies  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/search?q=\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\r\n  ac5b63f0  hubspot.companies  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/search?q=\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\r\n  bda8f5d7  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closedate=2026-07-01..2026-09-30&hs_is_closed_won=true\r\n  b9f81aaf  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?!amount?&closedate=2026-07-01..2026-09-30&hs_is_closed_won=true\r\n  dd9b00a7  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?!hubspot_owner_id?&closedate=2026-07-01..2026-09-30&hs_is_closed_won=true\r\n  b48b7857  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?!num_associated_contacts?&closedate=2026-07-01..2026-09-30&hs_is_closed_won=true\r\n\r\nphase breakdown (122s wall, 120s measured)\r\n  phase        calls  seconds  share    mean  tokens\r\n  survey           1     12.1   10%    12.1  no model call\r\n  recall           1    0.029    0%   0.029  no model call\r\n  loop_model       6     42.7   35%     7.1  in 12 out 3,507 cached 84,511\r\n  loop_tools       5      9.8    8%     2.0  no model call\r\n  draft            1     41.2   34%    41.2  in 30,040 out 4,182\r\n  gate             1    0.029    0%   0.029  no model call\r\n  verify           1      8.2    7%     8.2  in 31,085 out 1,393\r\n  sufficiency      1      6.3    5%     6.3  in 7,460 out 410\r\n  unmeasured              2.1    2%\r\n  cache hit rate: 55%\r\n"]
